    "reason": "The assertion that quantization lowers the numerical precision of model weights is factually sound. Quantization involves mapping a large set of values to a smaller set (e.g., reducing 32-bit floats to 8-bit integers), which inherently reduces the number of bits used to represent each weight, thereby decreasing the resolution or precision with which weights can be stored and computed.",
